# CVE-2026-33671 — picomatch ReDoS
# Source: vendored copy inside next/dist/compiled/picomatch (Next.js 15.5.15)
# Fix: requires Next.js to update its bundled picomatch. Cannot be patched via
# pnpm overrides because Next compiles its own copy at npm-publish time.
# Tracked: ISSUES.md i-6 (next 15 -> 16 bump deferred to v0.5).
CVE-2026-33671

# CVE-2026-42577: Netty epoll transport RST denial of service
#
# Affected artifact: io.netty:netty-transport-native-epoll
# Current version: 4.1.133.Final (via Spring Boot 3.5.x BOM)
# Fix version: 4.2.13.Final (no 4.1.x backport published)
#
# Justification:
# - This application uses Spring MVC on Tomcat (servlet stack), not WebFlux / Reactor Netty.
# - The netty-transport-native-epoll artifact is on the classpath transitively but never
#   touched by request-handling or outbound HTTP code paths in this app.
# - Bumping Netty to the 4.2.x major line creates Spring Boot 3.5.x compatibility risk
#   that is out of scope for a v0.5.0 hotfix.
# - Tracked for follow-up bump in v0.6 Phase 41 (security-hardening) as ISSUES.md i-14.
#
# Suppression entered: 2026-05-09 with v0.5.0 release.
CVE-2026-42577
